From: Edvanz Backend
Subject: [PATCH] PAY-016: re-price upcoming unpaid periods when a student's custom amount changes

REQ-PAY-016 / BR-PAY-003.

DEFECT
  SetCustomAmountAsync wrote StudentPaymentCounter.CustomPaymentAmount and nothing else.
  The only consumer of that field is OnStudentAssignedToSessionAsync, which pre-generates
  EVERY PaymentPeriod from the assignment month through session.EndDate in one shot. So a
  price change made AFTER enrolment (the actual tutor flow) had zero effect on any period,
  including future ones: GetStudentPaymentStatusAsync reported hasCustomAmount=true with a
  stale amountDue, and /collect still rejected the new price with
  PaymentAmountExceedsAdvanceLimit. TotalOutstanding was never reconciled either.

FIX (forward-only re-pricing)
  SetCustomAmountAsync becomes transactional. After writing the counter it re-prices the
  student's periods that (a) start on or after the current local month, (b) have received
  no cash (AmountPaid == 0), and (c) were not carried forward from another session, then
  adjusts TotalOutstanding by the delta.

  Deliberately NOT re-priced: settled months, partially-settled months, past months, and
  carried-forward balances — rewriting those would invalidate money already collected.
  A pro-rated first period keeps its ProRatedFraction; only the base amount changes
  (REQ-PAY-021/022).

  The response now carries the re-priced count so the UI can confirm the change landed,
  and PaymentStatusDto gains EffectiveAmount (the per-period price now in force) so the
  frontend never has to reconcile customAmount against amountDue itself.

NOT INCLUDED: Edvanz.Infrastructure/Repositories/PaymentRepo.cs — see the accompanying
notes; GetRepriceablePeriodsAsync must be appended to that class by hand.

